=== Mouse codon frequency comparison: BioMart CDS vs. Tim's data ===

[1] Parsing mouse CDS FASTA into a CSV table...
  Parsed 21,757 CDS records from /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/data/mouse_CDS_sequence.txt
  Saved to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/data/mouse_CDS_sequence.csv

[2] Computing codon frequencies from BioMart CDS sequences...
  Loaded 21,757 genes from /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/data/mouse_CDS_sequence.csv
  Dropped 80 genes with missing/unusable CDS sequences (not a multiple of 3, or too short); 21,677 genes remain.
  Saved BioMart codon frequencies to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/codon_frequencies_biomart_mouse.csv

[3] Loading Tim's codon frequencies and converting gene IDs...
  Loaded 20,611 genes from /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/data/LightStimPalAnnotations20211019_CDS_CodonFrequencies.csv (20,611 unique old IDs)
  252 of Tim's genes dropped: old ID maps to >1 distinct new gene ID.
  202 of Tim's genes dropped: old ID not found in the mapping table.
  67 of Tim's genes dropped: >1 of Tim's rows map to the same new gene ID (32 gene IDs affected).
  20,090 of Tim's 20,611 genes successfully converted to a unique new gene ID.

[4] Comparing BioMart vs. Tim's codon frequencies...
  19,948 genes with both BioMart and Tim codon frequencies.
  Saved per-codon comparison stats to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/codon_frequency_comparison_per_codon_mouse.csv
  Saved per-codon comparison stats (Spearman rho) to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/codon_frequency_comparison_per_codon_spearman_mouse.csv
  Saved per-gene comparison stats to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/codon_frequency_comparison_per_gene_mouse.csv

  Overall (all genes x all 61 codons, n=1,216,828): Pearson r = 0.9884 (p = 1.054e-996055), Spearman rho = 0.9879 (p = 2.947e-985675)
  Per-codon Pearson r: min = 0.9624 (AGG), median = 0.9807, max = 0.9926 (GGC)
  Per-gene total |difference| (summed over 61 codons): mean = 0.0253, median = 0.0030, 95th pct = 0.1432, max = 1.5351

[5] Plotting comparison figures...
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/codon_freq_biomart_vs_tim_overall_scatter_mouse.png  (Pearson R = 0.9884, p = 1.054e-996055)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/codon_freq_biomart_vs_tim_overall_scatter_spearman_mouse.png  (Spearman rho = 0.9879, p = 2.947e-985675)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/codon_freq_biomart_vs_tim_per_codon_pearson_r_mouse.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/codon_freq_biomart_vs_tim_per_codon_pearson_r_spearman_mouse.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/codon_freq_biomart_vs_tim_mean_codon_scatter_mouse.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/codon_freq_biomart_vs_tim_per_gene_diff_hist_mouse.png

[6] Loading mouse liver TE data...
  12,553 genes with TE_mean in /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_riboseq/tables/mouse_liver/mouse_te.csv
  12,258 genes with both BioMart codon frequencies and TE_mean.

[7] Fitting TE_mean ~ codon frequencies (BioMart) on autosomal genes...
  Training on 11,868 autosomal genes, 61 codon predictors.
  R^2 = 0.1435   Adjusted R^2 = 0.1391   n = 11868
  Saved intercept + 61 codon coefficients to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/co_mega_model_coefficients_mouse.csv
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_regression_fit_train_mouse.png  (Pearson R = 0.3789, Pearson R² = 0.1435, p = 1.075e-401, n = 11,868)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_regression_fit_train_spearman_mouse.png  (Spearman rho = 0.4072, Spearman rho² = 0.1658, p = 1.023e-469, n = 11,868)

[7b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Mouse liver) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=11,868): skew = -0.570, excess kurtosis = 1.114, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.8e-180, Jarque-Bera p = 1.54e-273
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.678, excess kurtosis = 1.852, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.57e-274, Jarque-Bera p = 0
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 224.985, p = 1.26e-20
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 28.472, p = 4.62e-13
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_mouse.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_histogram_mouse.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_qq_mouse.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_vs_fitted_mouse.png
  Saved diagnostic statistics to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_stats_mouse.csv

[8] Computing CO_Mega for all genes (autosomes + X) and comparing to TE...
  All genes with TE (n=12,258): Pearson r = 0.3784 (p = 0), Spearman rho = 0.4063 (p = 0)
  Autosomal genes only (n=11,868, training set): Pearson r = 0.3789 (p = 0), Spearman rho = 0.4072 (p = 0)
  X-linked genes only (n=374, held out): Pearson r = 0.3220 (p = 1.82e-10), Spearman rho = 0.3316 (p = 4.75e-11)
  Saved CO_Mega vs. TE correlation stats (n, Pearson r, p) to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/co_mega_te_correlation_stats_mouse.csv
  Saved CO_Mega vs. TE correlation stats (n, Spearman rho, p) to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/co_mega_te_correlation_stats_spearman_mouse.csv
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_vs_te_all_genes_mouse.png  (Pearson R = 0.3784, Pearson R² = 0.1432, p = 7.934e-414, n = 12,258)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_vs_te_all_genes_spearman_mouse.png  (Spearman rho = 0.4063, Spearman rho² = 0.1651, p = 1.295e-482, n = 12,258)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_vs_te_autosomal_mouse.png  (Pearson R = 0.3789, Pearson R² = 0.1435, p = 1.075e-401, n = 11,868)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_vs_te_autosomal_spearman_mouse.png  (Spearman rho = 0.4072, Spearman rho² = 0.1658, p = 1.023e-469, n = 11,868)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_vs_te_X_linked_mouse.png  (Pearson R = 0.3220, Pearson R² = 0.1037, p = 1.818e-10, n = 374)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/mouse/co_mega_vs_te_X_linked_spearman_mouse.png  (Spearman rho = 0.3316, Spearman rho² = 0.1100, p = 4.754e-11, n = 374)
  Saved CO_Mega for all 21,677 genes to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/mouse/co_mega_all_genes_mouse.csv

